# Site conventions

- Shared chrome (nav/footer) → `js/partials.js` custom elements.
- Shared visual patterns (hero shell, section container, eyebrows) → named classes in `css/style.css` (plain CSS; Tailwind CDN cannot `@apply` external stylesheets).
- Shared logic → modules like `js/utils.js`, `js/machine-card.js`.
- Page-only JS → `js/pages/`; page-only CSS → `css/pages/`, linked only from that page.
- Do not merge conceptually different UI into one class just because styles coincide today.
- Interactive state: one source of truth (prefer CSS classes toggled by JS).
- After changing shared CSS/JS referenced via `<link>`/`<script>`, bump the `?v=` cache-bust query on every page that loads them.
